Subject: [PATCH 6/7] touch-menu: add touch menu model, overlay rendering and
 tests

touch-menu: add touch menu model, overlay rendering and tests

A tablet or 2-in-1 without its keyboard has no way to leave a stream: the quit
shortcut and the gamepad chord need physical keys. Add the menu itself.

touchmenu.{h,cpp} is a pure class (gesture recognizer plus layout) with unit
tests: holding 3+ fingers still for 800 ms, a two-finger swipe from the right
edge (one finger from the right edge stays free for the host, three fingers
never reach the client on KDE) and a small corner handle that appears on touch
activity and hides after 6 s all open it; items are Disconnect, Quit session,
Toggle statistics and Close menu.

OverlayManager draws the menu on the existing bottom-left status overlay, which
every renderer already places 1:1, so no renderer changes are needed. The right
hand panel is a full-width surface that is transparent outside the panel;
renderers can opt out through supportsWideOverlay().

Not yet reachable: input handling and session wiring follow in the next patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
